  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Reducing Disaster Risk and Enhancing Emergency Preparedness in the COVID-19 context for Timor-Leste</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Considering Timor-Leste&#x2019;s vulnerability to natural disasters, and to address the needs demonstrated by Cyclone Seroja, IOM is supporting the Government of Timor-Leste in the enhancement of national and local capacities to reduce disaster risk and improve preparedness to future disasters. The project is focusing its efforts on enhancing Government capacity to reduce disaster risk and improve preparedness, including through non-food item prepositioning. In addition to this, the project ensures that populations vulnerable to disasters have safe spaces to shelter during disasters building on IOM and the shelter cluster&#x2019;s planned nationwide evacuation centre assessment and inventory. The project also plays a key role in supporting highly vulnerable communities to better prepare for future disasters through enhanced community preparedness and local-level early warning systems.</narrative>
  </description>
